WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.333
Orbit is a Python scientific calculator. Here it calculates and saves results to PostgreSQL.

2
00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:12.667
Degree mode returns sine of thirty as zero point five. The shared notebook persists calculations.

3
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:17.893
Sixty nine backend tests pass using isolated databases. Ruff also passes.

4
00:00:17.893 --> 00:00:22.360
More than ten meaningful commits, with secrets and generated files excluded.

5
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:27.713
Compose runs three healthy services: frontend, backend, and PostgreSQL.

6
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:33.179
Both application containers run as non-root users. The frontend uses a multi-stage build.

7
00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:40.265
GitHub Actions passes tests, builds, security scans, container publication, and a real cluster check.

8
00:00:40.265 --> 00:00:45.465
Backend images are published to GitHub Container Registry with exact commit SHA tags.

9
00:00:45.465 --> 00:00:50.398
The frontend has matching immutable SHA tags, rather than a moving latest tag.

10
00:00:50.398 --> 00:00:54.335
Trivy finds no high or critical vulnerabilities in the backend image.

11
00:00:54.335 --> 00:00:58.668
The frontend scan also passes. Either scan can block publication.

12
00:00:58.668 --> 00:01:03.603
Terraform plans twenty real resources in Mumbai, including the VPC and EKS.

13
00:01:03.603 --> 00:01:09.203
Apply completes successfully: twenty resources added. These are original captured results.

14
00:01:09.203 --> 00:01:14.003
The AWS Console shows the provisioned project VPC in ap-south-one.

15
00:01:14.003 --> 00:01:17.403
Two public subnets span separate availability zones.

16
00:01:17.403 --> 00:01:20.403
The EKS control plane is active in the same region.

17
00:01:20.403 --> 00:01:24.603
Two worker nodes are Ready. This is the actual captured EKS Console.

18
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:29.803
Helm manages the application, Ingress controller, and monitoring releases on EKS.

19
00:01:29.803 --> 00:01:34.634
Two backend and two frontend replicas are Running, alongside PostgreSQL.

20
00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:39.195
ClusterIP Services expose both application tiers inside Kubernetes.

21
00:01:39.195 --> 00:01:43.754
Ingress routes the root to the frontend, and API requests to FastAPI.

22
00:01:43.754 --> 00:01:48.420
The metrics endpoint exposes real Prometheus request and latency measurements.

23
00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.366
Prometheus scrapes both backend replicas. Both targets are UP.

24
00:01:52.366 --> 00:01:57.233
Grafana displays populated live request, latency, and error panels.

25
00:01:57.233 --> 00:02:02.523
After the successful pipeline, a local Helm upgrade deploys the exact published commit.

26
00:02:02.523 --> 00:02:08.323
The health endpoint reports that commit, and the saved notebook survives pod replacement.

27
00:02:08.323 --> 00:02:15.463
Terraform destroy removes the remaining resources. AWS evidence is historical; the infrastructure is now deleted.

28
00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:22.063
An independent audit confirms no project cluster, VPC, volumes, or active workers remain.

29
00:02:22.063 --> 00:02:28.937
Temporary credentials are removed. README links all screenshots, source logs, and the original live recording.

